      "id": 1,
      "text": "West Grove’s name comes from the Friends Meeting House on Harmony Road built in 1787.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Grove%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1868 Charles Dingee and Alfred Conard founded Dingee & Conard Nursery, the largest rose nursery in the U.S.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Grove%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "West Grove incorporated on November 29, 1893, but the decree was recorded January 9, 1894 to avoid tax confusion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Grove%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first council meeting took place March 6, 1894 in the Library Room of the National Bank Building on Exchange Place.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Grove%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1885 the Daily Local News called West Grove “one of the most flourishing villages in this county” and noted its large rose nursery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Grove%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Joseph Pyle, known as the “Father of West Grove,” built the oldest brick structure in town and helped finance the 1885 casket factory.",
